# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-4, R-11). L §2.3: def = "def" ID [binds] ":" type "=" (expr | hole) ["at" lawdate] NL
# {IN "note" STR NL}; L §2.4: "A one-line def followed by note lines means the long form, the same def with its one
# rule labelled base and those notes" (2.0: a parse failure). rate is its row carried through.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input r: num
def rate: num = r at reader
  note "the rate the bank states"
ask q: rate law 2026-06-30

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r = 0.05
=== expect
q: 0.05
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
